        "ImageDescription": {
          "value": "City of Vancouver FIREBOAT 1 (FB-1), going under Lion’s Gate Bridge from Burrard Inlet into Vancouver Harbor, Vancouver, British Columbia, Canada on August 31, 2018. <br>\n<p>FIREBOAT 1 (FB-1) is FireStorm 40 built by MetalCraft Marine, one of two fireboats purchased by the City of Vancouver in 2016. <br>\nAs noted in Wikipedia topic – “Fireboats of Vancouver”, there are 2 generations of “FIREBOAT 1” fire fighting vessels for the city of Vancouver, BC Canada. <br>\n</p>\nIn 2016, the original FIREBOAT 1 (gray hull with red stripe) was replaced by FIREBOAT 1 (FB-1) (white top/red bottom). It has an “FB-1” painted on the bow and number “89001” on the hull in a couple of places. Unfortunately, the City of Vancouver does not use an additional identifying universal number such as IMO, ENI or MMSI with their firefighting vessels. <br>",
          "source": "commons-desc-page"
        },
